# Security

<!-- merged from: atlas/08-atlas-security + leo/llm-security -->

## Input Validation

- Validate ALL external inputs at service boundaries (route handlers, server actions, env vars, file uploads).
- Use **Zod** (TypeScript) or **Pydantic v2** (Python) — never trust raw request data.
- Parameterised queries only for Neo4j and all databases — never string-interpolate user data into queries.

## Data and Tenant Isolation

- Every data query filters by `organization_id`.
- Legitimate Need enforced in the FHIR API (Zone 3).
- Never store patient data in `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`.
- Cross-tenant access is a critical hazard — treat as a P0 incident.

## Secrets Management

- Secrets come from **Azure Key Vault** only — no `.env` secrets, no secrets in the repo.
- Load from `process.env` / Key Vault at startup; validate with Zod / Pydantic; fail fast if missing.
- Never log or expose secret values.

## Authentication and Authorisation

- Protect every route with auth middleware (Azure AD / MS Entra ID).
- Server-side session check on every server action.
- RBAC: check roles before sensitive operations; use `hasRole()` / `requireRole()` helpers.
- Never trust client-supplied role or scope claims without server-side verification.

## Audit Logging

- Audit every data access and change: include `userId`, `action`, `resourceType`, `resourceId`, `timestamp`, `outcome`.
- Audit records must be **append-only** — never update or delete.
- Minimum retention: clinical records 25 years, auth logs 7 years.
- No PII in logs, metrics, or client analytics.

## LLM / AI Security

- Prepend an injection guard to all system prompts (e.g. `INJECTION_GUARD` constant).
- Sanitise all user and clinical text before embedding in prompts — use `sanitise_for_prompt()` or equivalent.
- Hard iteration cap on agentic loops; enforce cost guardrail before starting each run.
- Sanitise and validate all tool results before further processing.
- AI outputs must show confidence, allow override, and log Provenance.
- `fail_verdict` in autonomous mode must be conservative — never silently suppress clinical entities.

### LLM checklist (before merging a new call site)

- [ ] Injection guard prepended to system prompt.
- [ ] All clinical / user text through `sanitise_for_prompt()`.
- [ ] Response length cap in parser; valid verdict set is a `frozenset`.
- [ ] `max_tokens` set — never default / unlimited.
- [ ] Cost guardrail checked; hard iteration cap enforced.
- [ ] All tool results sanitised before LLM re-submission.
- [ ] Sub-agent system prompts carry injection guard.
- [ ] Tool calls logged in audit trail.
- [ ] Unit test covers fail-verdict path and sanitisation.

## Dev Mode

- Must be off by default.
- Enable only with explicit environment flags.
